# OneBrain — secrets template.
# Copy to ~/.secrets/.env (chmod 600) and fill in real values.
# NOTHING in this file should ever be committed. The scripts read these at runtime;
# no token value is ever stored in the OneBrain repo itself.

# --- gbrain auth tokens (generate your own random strings) ---
# Admin bootstrap token: used by `gbrain serve` to mint/verify auth. Keep private.
GBRAIN_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=

# Remote/client bearer token: what each AI agent (Claude, Codex, Grok, gateway)
# presents to the local MCP endpoint. Loopback-only, but still bearer-gated.
GBRAIN_REMOTE_TOKEN=

# Desktop/Cowork bridge token (optional): used by the Claude Desktop stdio->HTTP bridge.
GBRAIN_DESKTOP_TOKEN=

# --- paths ---
# Absolute path to your Obsidian vault (the single source of truth).
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=$HOME/Obsidian/YourVault

# Absolute path to your local gbrain checkout.
GBRAIN_REPO=$HOME/Code/gbrain

# Absolute path to the shared Agent Lessons note (append target for nightly capture).
# install.sh / setup detect an existing "Agent Lessons.md" anywhere in the vault and
# pin this automatically. Default if none exists:
#   $OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH/30 Areas/AI & Systems/Agent Lessons.md
# Do NOT leave this pointing at a missing path while another Agent Lessons.md exists —
# that split-brains the log (the job still exits ok; the sentinel cannot catch it).
# ONEBRAIN_LESSONS_NOTE=$HOME/Obsidian/YourVault/30 Areas/AI & Systems/Agent Lessons.md

# IMPORTANT: do NOT set OPENAI_API_KEY here if you want 100% offline embeddings.
# OneBrain uses local Ollama (nomic-embed-text). The scripts actively unset
# OPENAI_API_KEY so nothing silently falls back to a paid cloud embedding API.

# --- notifications (optional; ~/.onebrain/notify.env, chmod 600) -------------
# OneBrain's notifier reaches you when the brain degrades or a lesson is captured.
# gbrain itself has no notification layer, so this lives in the wrapper.
# Every channel is optional and no-ops silently if unset.
#
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN   create a bot with @BotFather, copy the token it gives you
#   TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID     message @userinfobot to get your own ID; for a group,
#                        forward one of its messages to @userinfobot (negative number)
#
# Verify with:  ~/.gbrain/bin/onebrain-notify.sh "test" "OneBrain"
# A token that is PRESENT and a token that WORKS are different states. Send the
# test and confirm you received it before considering setup done.
